[0.108, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mnager (the UI registers their loader; `UiSystem` takes the manager as an optional last argument, the sh\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mell passes its own). Until an image arrives its element draws without it, laid out as if it had no size\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m, so an element whose style fixes its size does not move; the frame it arrives on RmlUi is asked again \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mand draws it. A missing or undecodable image is logged once and stays blank; a decorator's image, and e\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mvery image of a UI with no manager, is still decoded on the main thread. The loads count in `ResourceMa\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mnager::Loading`, so the reference views and screenshots wait for them as for a scene's models; the twel\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mve reference views are unchanged to the pixel. Exit criterion met: the ui suite shows an image decoded \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mon the worker drawn once ready, through a document read again, and a missing or broken one logged once \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mand blank. [UI](ui.md#the-game-ui) |                                                                   \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m  2 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mFree: parked on feature-base. J14 (images off-thread) merged 2026-11-28, awaiting the batch gate.      \r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[39mSearchin\u001b[12G for \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m patt\u0